# Development instructions

**The stack's rules live in the dev skill**, `.claude/skills/dev/SKILL.md`
([readable on GitHub](https://github.com/joeblew999/dev/blob/main/skills/dev/SKILL.md)) —
linked by mise from the pinned `dev` release, generated from the tool's own
verbs, and the one source of what the tool does and the rules it keeps:
nothing personal in git, secrets only through fnox, every error names its fix,
tests and releases the same locally and in GitHub Actions. Load it before
build, test, release or deploy. This file says only what is about this repo.

## Rule zero: nothing to remember

- **Every workflow is a mise task.** `mise tasks` lists them. Do not document or
  rely on raw `go`, `wrangler`, `flyctl` or `fnox` commands; if a workflow is
  missing, add a task. A task is one line in `mise.toml`; anything with a
  branch, a loop, a parse or an API call belongs in the `dev` tool
  (`github.com/joeblew999/dev`), with a test, never in a shell script behind a
  task.
- **hk owns the checks.** `mise run lint` runs them; the pre-commit hook and
  the Claude Code Stop hook run the same, so `hk run check` must stay cheap.
  The expensive, login-gated `session:verify` is bound to pre-push only.

## Working rules

- **Nothing outside this repo.** No global Claude Code skills, plugins, memory
  or settings, and no files left in temp or home directories.
- **Skills are pinned, synced by mise, and proven to load.** A packslip tool's
  skill arrives with its pin; anything else is a `[source.*]` in
  `session.toml`. The PreToolUse hook `.claude/hooks/skill-gate` loads the
  right one before a write; `mise run hooks:check` proves it.
- **Use tools the way their authors document them.**
- **Once something works, put it in mise and the plan.** No manual steps.
- **One-time, per machine:** mise lists a packslip tool's releases through
  GitHub's API, anonymously unless it has a token, and gh keeps its token in
  the keyring where mise cannot read it. Tell mise once, in your own global
  settings (a project may not):
  `mise settings set github.credential_command "gh auth token"`.
- **Test for real before saying done**, and say plainly what could not be.
- **Prove a hello world round trip in every topology** before building on it.
- **Commit only files you name.** Never `git add -A`.

## Layout

| Path | Owns |
|---|---|
| `cmd/__NAME__` | the first command, its own Go module: `main.go`, and beside it a `wrangler.toml` or `fly.toml` once it deploys |
| `go.work` | the one file at the root that knows Go: every command's module |
| `mise.toml` | every task; the stack half is identical across repos, the project half is a line per command and stage |
| `session.toml` | what this repo pins of its Claude Code session |
| `.claude/skills/SESSION.lock` | every skill a session here is allowed to have; `mise run session:verify --update` records it |
| `skills/` | any skill this repo's releases ship via packslip |
